<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<topic id="ac8cf6b9-a48f-4b86-b13d-2303a63255aa" revisionNumber="1">
  <developerConceptualDocument
    xmlns="http://ddue.schemas.microsoft.com/authoring/2003/5"
    xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink">

    <introduction>
      <para>The following samples showcase some of the functionality in DemiCode Scheduler.</para>
    </introduction>

	
									
	
		
			
			
			
            
            
            
<section>
  <title>In this section</title>
  <content>
    <para>   <definitionTable>
                    <definedTerm><link xlink:href="0f5a09a1-60d5-4059-8bae-075eaf192191" /></definedTerm>
                    <definition>
                        The SchedulerConsole project shows a regular Console application using DemiCode Scheduler to output messages to the console.</definition>
                        
                    <definedTerm><link xlink:href="f0361e4e-a359-4f54-a200-6e8a11b94dff" /></definedTerm>
                    <definition>
                        The SchedulerService project shows a Windows Service using DemiCode Scheduler to log information to the Application event log.</definition>
                        
                        <definedTerm><link xlink:href="345714a3-e403-4388-8cba-619008e75b6f" /></definedTerm>
                    <definition>
                        The <codeEntityReference qualifyHint="false">T:DemiCode.Scheduling.Tasks.ApplicationTask</codeEntityReference> is part of the task system in DemiCode Scheduler. 
                        This sample shows how the ApplicationTask is implemented and is usefull as a starting point for implementing your own tasks.</definition>

                    <definedTerm>
                      <link xlink:href="7451DB08-3678-4263-BF51-AB5D88E6E93C" />
                    </definedTerm>
                    <definition>
                      The SchedulerConfiguration project shows a .NET WinForms application that reads configuration files, dislays configuration controls and writes changes 
                      back to disk.
                    </definition>
      
                </definitionTable>
			
            
            Additional samples will be made available at <externalLink>
  <linkText>www.demicode.com/products/scheduler/samples</linkText>
  <linkUri>http://www.demicode.com/products/scheduler/samples</linkUri>
  <linkTarget>_blank</linkTarget>
</externalLink>. Check our site regularly for tips, tricks and code.</para>
  </content>
</section>

            
             
            
		
			
				
		
	
    

